---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>
  <header
    class='px-6 sm:px-8 pt-20 sm:pt-24 lg:pt-32 md:px-20 md:pt-42 max-w-screen-xl'
  >
    <h1
      class='text-slate-200 text-4xl flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl xl:text-[95px] text-left max-w-screen-md'
    >
      <span class='animate-fade-in-up'>Sensationally</span>
      <span class='animate-fade-in-up'>Awkward</span>
    </h1>
  </header>
  <article
    class='max-w-screen-sm pl-6 sm:pl-8 md:pl-20 pr-4 mt-6 md:mt-8 space-y-4 mb-20'
  >
    <p
      class='text-slate-300 3xl:text-lg text-pretty animate-fade-in-up'
      style={{ animationDelay: "300ms", animationFillMode: "both" }}
    >
      When I was 6, a young man in a white rolled-up shirt and black trousers
      came to my school to tell us about computers. He called himself <b
        >"Mr Speak-up"</b
      > and said the computer was a magical device that could teach you anything.
      He told us about <strong>Bill Gates</strong>, the creator of Windows, and
      how one invention changed the world. I left with more questions than I
      could hold.
    </p>
    <p
      class='text-slate-300 3xl:text-lg text-pretty animate-fade-in-up'
      style={{ animationDelay: "400ms", animationFillMode: "both" }}
    >
      By 2006, I was in primary 4 and I had an exciting computer teacher. His
      name was Mr. Lawrence. He really loved computers and he inspired me to
      love them too. He then thought us about the web and said the internet us a
      gateway to endless possibilities. From that day, I became fascinated by
      the endless possibilities the internet offered. Starting my journey into
      building things on for the internet.
      <p
        class='text-slate-300 3xl:text-lg text-pretty animate-fade-in-up'
        style={{ animationDelay: "500ms", animationFillMode: "both" }}
      >
        My parents had a desktop computer at home, and I would spend hours
        tinkering with it, trying to figure out how it worked. I played with
        Microsoft Paint, Publisher, Word and Corel Draw. The first time I played
        with the internet, I was amazed by the vast amount of information
        available.
      </p>
      <p
        class='text-slate-300 3xl:text-lg text-pretty animate-fade-in-up'
        style={{ animationDelay: "500ms", animationFillMode: "both" }}
      >
        "That's not going to take away what the team has done and the boys have
        done in the last six or seven weeks since coming back from the World
        Cup," said boss Mikel Arteta. "What we've done, the way we've competed
        and the amount of games we've won has been remarkable - but this is a
        big lesson for all of us to understand what it takes to win at this
        level."
      </p>
      <p
        class='text-slate-300 3xl:text-lg text-pretty animate-fade-in-up'
        style={{ animationDelay: "500ms", animationFillMode: "both" }}
      >
        "That's not going to take away what the team has done and the boys have
        done in the last six or seven weeks since coming back from the World
        Cup," said boss Mikel Arteta. "What we've done, the way we've competed
        and the amount of games we've won has been remarkable - but this is a
        big lesson for all of us to understand what it takes to win at this
        level."
      </p>
    </p>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
